note search <regex>: a Rust regex over every line the index holds in memory, printed as file:line: text. The agent reaches for it to find code it cannot yet name a symbol for (browsing search). The regex is compiled in the query arm first, so a bad pattern is an error before anything is scanned. It reads the same files the index walked, so ignored and non-indexed files are not searched.

